hich is  Donald Trump's tariffs so let's start  with the first issue Donald Trump after  begging for rate cuts and getting one  ended not boosting stocks and in fact  coinciding with the decrease came out  and said well okay the  reason that this rate cut didn't work  the way I expected was while the Fed did  do a rate cut they didn't do a bigger  rate cut which is what I really wanted  and they also didn't pair the rate cut  with a statement that they're gonna  continue doing further cuts so they're  just not sending a clear enough signal  about how great the economy is and is  going to be so we don't really need to  talk much more about that it's Trump  logic which is also known as anti logic  I mean it truly makes no sense  whatsoever and it is one of these things  of Donald Trump post facto coming up  with rationalizations that nothing  beyond a five-year-old or a hyper  partisan Republican would fall for so  then we get to more generally do rate  cuts actually stimulate the economy and  there's a really interesting article in  The New York Times which says that  lately no rate cuts don't really help  anymore in the modern economy the normal  sort of mechanism is you cut the federal  funds rate and this will lead to  Americans buying more durable goods like  cars and such it will drop interest  rates on mortgages so people will start  refinancing their homes they will lower  their payments and have more money freed  up to spend on other stuff so it's great  for the economy in that way there are  some other mechanisms but for the  consumer facing analysis that that's the  primary analysis but there's a different  modern economy now that we're in the  reality is the modern economy doesn't  really work this way people don't just  save save save and then when there's a  rate cut go out and do a ton of spending  spending has a much more sort of natural  cycle and then in addition to that  remember the bottom 50% of the economy  has stagnant wages they've had stagnant  wages for decades they just can't afford  it to do much more buying because the  Fed Funds rate went down 25 basis points  so primarily it is a method that ties  into big finance and for the run-up of  stock markets which again only benefit a  certain portion of the economy low rates  won't do much if people don't have money  so the long and short of it is that even  this reliance on rate cuts to jumpstart  economies or to prevent recessions  that's old economic thinking and of  course it's based on a neck  status quo that was never good for most  people anyway of indefinite growth as  the goal and such a such a sort of  divergence between the benefits to the  top 1% and 10% and 50% and almost  nothing for the bottom 50% so that's a  bigger conversation to be had but then  here's the real elephant in the room  completely missing from Trump getting  his rate cut and stocks crashing Trump  furious that a 25 basis point rate cut  didn't jump-start the stock market  consider that the same day that the rate  funds rate that the funds rate was cut  Trump announced two even more  destructive tariffs which are terrible  for the United States take a look at  this Trump on Twitter our  representatives have just returned from  China where they had constructive talks  having to do with the future trade deal  we thought we had a deal with China  three months ago but sadly China decided  to renegotiate the deal prior to signing  more recently China agreed to buy  agricultural products from the US and  large quantities but did not do so  additionally my friend my friend  President Xi said that he would stop the  sale of fentanyl to the United States  this never happened and Americans  continue to die trade talks are  continuing and during the talks the US  will start on September 1st putting a  small additional tariff of 10% on the  remaining 300 billion dollars of goods  and products coming from China into our  country this does not include the two  hundred and fifty billion dollars  already tariffed at 25 percent so the  entire conversation all along trump so  reliant on the federal funds rate which  increasingly does not generate the  economic reaction that it once used to  or was believed to Trump talking about  the rate decrease wasn't big enough the  messaging from the Fed wasn't strong  enough about how great the economy is  and that there will be subsequent rate  cuts that entire discussion was a farce  Trump wanted a rate cut and he got it  and stocks crashed well the problem is  not that the cut wasn't big enough the  New York Times explains the rate cuts in  general are less connected to immediate  stock market gains but nowhere in that  entire back-and-forth is the reality  that the same day that Trump announced  more tariffs that are terrible for  American company  and Americans at large the stock market  started to crash and is down as of right  now might be different by the time it  closes we're filming before the close of  the stock market today the Dow is down  an additional nearly 600 points as usual  Donald Trump's propagandizing combined  with a very poor understanding of basic  economics and the totally missing story  of the tariffs ends up with completely  wrong headlines related to what's  happening in our economy and of course  people fall for it and they say yes the  problem is what Trump says the problem  is not stagnant wages for 40 years  it's that liberal lefty biased Federal  Reserve that just won't give Donald  Trump a bigger rate cut Trump is the  victim as usual one of the things that  Trump has in common with many other  authoritarians regularly framing himself  as the victim I will be talking much  more about this actually Wednesday  evening I will be having a live stream  on Twitch at 6:30 p.m. Eastern Time we  will be talking about this and many  other economic issues follow me there  twitch.tv slash David Pakman and join me  Wednesday evening 6:30 p.m. Eastern

